"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. The project kicked off on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the lead and an initial budget of $500,000 for phase one. The executive board later approved a total budget of $2 million to cover research, development, and marketing. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th, and a breakthrough in predictive analytics during phase two, with a detailed report scheduled for November 20th. The team has expanded with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions held in September and earlier in April for external partners. Strategic partnerships have been established, including a collaboration with TechInnovate for AI research. The project is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience by the end of November."
